Subject: JS_ComputeMemoryUsage does not read class data of a plain object

What this does
  - `JS_ComputeMemoryUsage` has a case for `JS_CLASS_OBJECT` that counts nothing, ahead of the default case.

Why we need it
  The default case treated `p->u.opaque` as an allocated block. A plain object has no class data, and an object made with inline property room is allocated as `offsetof(JSObject, u) + cap * sizeof(JSProperty)`: its `u` area is the first property slots (or nothing, when the capacity is zero), so the read took a property value for a pointer or ran past the allocation.

Failure
  `CDPTest.EveryAdvertisedMethodIsImplemented` (`Runtime.getHeapUsage` through `JS_ComputeMemoryUsage`) reported a heap-buffer-overflow of 8 bytes at the `p->u.opaque` read under AddressSanitizer on Linux (the ASan ctest of the checkpoint run, finding F11).

Soundness
  - Memory statistics only; no allocation, ownership or object state changes.
  - Other classes keep their cases.

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -12128,0 +12129,2 @@
+            break;
+        case JS_CLASS_OBJECT:            /* no class data: the union is not used */
